  "body": "Part of #290 (design decisions D1-D10 in its research comment).\n\nDepends on: #531.\n\nThe first wire op (D1). A vertical cut along a contour:\n- offset by the wire radius plus the condition's gap;\n- explicit **punch / die** side parameter, never inferred (folded in per D8);\n- lead-in/out from a stated **start hole / threading point**;\n- **corner strategy:** minimum internal radius is wire radius + gap, and a smaller corner is refused by name (folded in per D8).\n\nMoves carry no pose, so the cut posts as XY (D2). Refusals: an enclosed profile without a start hole; a missing wire diameter, gap or condition (at command creation).\n\n**Done means:** a die and a punch on the same profile offset to opposite sides by exactly the kerf. A too-tight corner and a missing start hole are refused by name. CL golden committed.",
